WEBVTT

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:08.065
When diplomacy fails,

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:10.474
there's only one alternative...

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.239
violence.

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:16.180
Force must be applied
without apology.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:22.254
It's the Starfleet way.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:24.882
Then our philosophies
are in agreement.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.653
Will you help us?

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:30.026
You're asking me
to fight your war,

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:32.793
destroy your enemy.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:34.732
L'm asking you
to intimidate the Kyrians

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:36.258
with your technology...

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.566
help me capture their leader.

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:41.233
This ship
has superior firepower.

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:43.435
He won't risk a conflict
with you.

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:47.537
We risk life and limb

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:52.017
so your people
can annex Kyrian land.

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:54.612
Sounds like a good deal for you.

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:56.281
What do we get?

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.916
A way home.

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:03.419
You know more about Voyager
than you've let on.

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:06.489
Your reputation
in this Quadrant precedes you.

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:08.433
That's why we sought you out.

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:09.799
L'm listening.

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:14.034
There's a cyclic wormhole
five days' journey from here.

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.598
We know where it is

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:18.236
and we can help you
stabilize it.

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:24.443
If you are lying...

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:27.851
How far do you have to go?

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.754
60,000 light-years?

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:35.784
L want all tactical data
regarding your little war:

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:38.889
Kyrian defenses,
the position of your own forces,

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.091
everything.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:43.000
You'll have it within the hour.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.832
Eight Kyrian fighter-ships
approaching.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.105
Arm the assault probes.

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:52.441
Fire at will.

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:53.776
Hail them.

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.508
Channel open.

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:59.848
This is Captain Janeway
of the Warship Voyager.

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:02.116
Break off your attack,
or l'll destroy you.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:04.282
They are not responding.

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:08.487
They're returning fire.

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:09.859
Shields are holding.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:12.797
Chako-tay, any luck
tracking down their leader?

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:14.231
Not yet.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.666
We think Tedran has
gone into hiding.

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:16.669
L thought he might.

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.762
We'll have to flush him out.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.602
What do you suggest?

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.768
Biogenic weapons.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.334
We'll infect

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:28.677
the most populated
Kyrian territories.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:31.878
The Doctor's nearly done
working on the weapon.

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:36.184
Our conflict is with Tedran
himself, not with his people.

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:37.280
They're innocent.

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.688
The best way
to bring down a ruler

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.056
is to make his people suffer.

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:41.390
- Captain...
- This is no time

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:42.394
for half-measures.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:44.794
You wanted victory.

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:45.991
You're going to get it.

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.023
Bridge to Sick Bay.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.364
Status?

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:51.529
We have established
a datalink

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:53.903
between my neural net
and the phaser array.

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:55.463
L am reconfiguring the beam

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:58.875
to carry a bio-agent
into the planet's atmosphere.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:01.312
When will it be ready?

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.975
Lt is ready now, Captain.

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:06.417
Phasers are on line.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.443
Target the first city.

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:11.554
And fire.

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.602
The Warship Voyager...

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:26.833
one of the most powerful vessels
of its time.

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:30.604
Armed with photonic torpedoes
and particle weapons,

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:31.974
this ship of destruction

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:35.037
could wipe out an entire
civilization within hours.

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:37.709
On this particular day
in history, we were lucky.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.877
The death toll
could've been much worse.

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:42.387
By the time Voyager
targeted our major cities,

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:45.186
Tedran had already begun
an evacuation.

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:47.022
Thousands of lives were saved.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.425
Unfortunately, it was
only the beginning

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:51.191
of Captain Janeway's onslaught.

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:52.391
As you'll see,

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:56.391
her actions would have a
lasting effect on our world.

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:59.098
Even today, 700 years later,

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:04.804
we are still feeling the impact
of the Voyager encounter.

00:05:54.785 --> 00:05:57.049
Before we continue
the simulation,

00:05:57.088 --> 00:05:59.886
l'd like to answer
any questions you might have.

00:05:59.957 --> 00:06:02.585
L'm curious
about Voyager itself.

00:06:02.627 --> 00:06:04.254
How many people were on board?

00:06:04.295 --> 00:06:05.922
We believe
they had a complement

00:06:05.963 --> 00:06:08.431
of over 300 soldiers.

00:06:08.466 --> 00:06:10.525
Did they attack
other worlds, as well?

00:06:10.568 --> 00:06:12.798
Well, we aren't certain.

00:06:12.837 --> 00:06:15.101
Records of Voyager's travels
through our Quadrant

00:06:15.139 --> 00:06:17.300
are incomplete,
but it's safe to assume

00:06:17.341 --> 00:06:20.538
that they interfered
with many other cultures, yes.

00:06:20.578 --> 00:06:22.205
Tell us more
about the Borg drones

00:06:22.246 --> 00:06:23.440
they kept on the ship.

00:06:23.481 --> 00:06:26.006
Voyager had many weapons
at their disposal,

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:29.042
including species they'd
assimilated along the way:

00:06:29.086 --> 00:06:31.987
Borg, Talaxian, Kazon.

00:06:32.023 --> 00:06:33.354
They were captured
and made to work

00:06:33.391 --> 00:06:34.756
as part of Voyager's
fighting force.

00:06:34.792 --> 00:06:36.555
Let's resume the simulation,

00:06:36.594 --> 00:06:38.562
and you can see for yourself.

00:06:40.998 --> 00:06:43.432
It's a few hours after
the initial bombardment.

00:06:43.467 --> 00:06:45.128
Janeway and her squadron
are on the Bridge,

00:06:45.169 --> 00:06:46.636
mounting their assault.

00:06:46.671 --> 00:06:51.802
Now, what you are about to see
is graphic and unsettling.

00:06:53.044 --> 00:06:54.671
Status.

00:06:54.712 --> 00:06:56.646
Status!

00:06:56.681 --> 00:06:58.444
Approximately
3,000 Kyrians dead.

00:06:58.482 --> 00:06:59.449
That's it?

00:06:59.483 --> 00:07:01.451
The bio-agent
is still dispersing

00:07:01.485 --> 00:07:02.679
through the atmosphere.

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:06.247
The fatality rate
will be 300,000 soon enough.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:07.450
How soon?

00:07:07.491 --> 00:07:08.788
Best guess...

00:07:08.826 --> 00:07:10.123
one hour.

00:07:10.161 --> 00:07:13.028
Why do you always
keep me waiting, Tuvok?

00:07:14.532 --> 00:07:16.193
My apologies.

00:07:16.233 --> 00:07:18.463
Preparing to fire again.

00:07:18.502 --> 00:07:21.130
Double the yield.

00:07:21.172 --> 00:07:23.970
Captain, don't you think
that's excessive?

00:07:24.008 --> 00:07:25.407
You picked a bad time

00:07:25.443 --> 00:07:27.843
to have second thoughts,
Ambassador.

00:07:27.912 --> 00:07:30.107
L want them defeated,

00:07:30.147 --> 00:07:33.310
but... but this is genocide.

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:34.977
Defeat? Genocide?

00:07:35.019 --> 00:07:37.146
Why quibble with semantics?

00:07:37.188 --> 00:07:39.884
This wasn't our agreement.

00:07:42.359 --> 00:07:44.486
We're going to defeat
the Kyrians

00:07:44.528 --> 00:07:48.020
and you're going to keep up
your end of the bargain.

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:57.070
Ensign, confine
this gentleman to the brig.

00:07:57.108 --> 00:07:58.735
L'll let you know
when it's over.

00:08:03.614 --> 00:08:06.981
Three more Kyrian vessels
approaching.

00:08:07.017 --> 00:08:08.314
Evade them.

00:08:08.352 --> 00:08:09.683
Aye, aye, sir.

00:08:18.395 --> 00:08:20.090
The location?

00:08:22.099 --> 00:08:24.693
Look... l can keep
this up all day.

00:08:24.735 --> 00:08:27.863
Tell the Commander
what he wants to know.

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:38.144
Maybe l can't keep
this up all day.

00:08:38.182 --> 00:08:40.616
L'm a man of peace.

00:08:40.651 --> 00:08:43.677
My native people
are enlightened...

00:08:43.721 --> 00:08:45.086
nonviolent...

00:08:45.122 --> 00:08:46.612
much like your own.

00:08:46.657 --> 00:08:50.058
L'm saddened that this
has happened to you.

00:08:51.562 --> 00:08:53.757
If we can work together,

00:08:53.798 --> 00:08:56.733
maybe we can end
this conflict.

00:08:56.767 --> 00:08:58.166
Stand aside, Chako-tay.

00:08:58.202 --> 00:08:59.499
Let me hit him.

00:08:59.537 --> 00:09:03.530
That hyperspanner would cause
an unacceptable level of damage.

00:09:03.574 --> 00:09:07.066
L remind you...
he must still be able to speak.

00:09:09.079 --> 00:09:11.912
What do you have in mind?

00:09:11.949 --> 00:09:13.439
This neural solvent...

00:09:13.484 --> 00:09:16.180
a clean and efficient
inducer of pain...

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:17.517
far more effective

00:09:17.555 --> 00:09:20.388
than your crude
attempts at persuasion.

00:09:22.993 --> 00:09:26.724
No doubt you are experiencing
a tingling sensation

00:09:26.764 --> 00:09:28.061
behind your eyes.

00:09:28.098 --> 00:09:30.999
The chemical is dissolving
your optic nerves.

00:09:31.035 --> 00:09:33.026
L'll ask you again.

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:34.662
Where is Tedran?

00:09:34.705 --> 00:09:38.835
The pain will increase
exponentially

00:09:38.876 --> 00:09:41.436
until your cerebral
cortex begins to liquefy.

00:09:41.478 --> 00:09:43.412
L can reverse the process...

00:09:43.447 --> 00:09:45.312
if ordered to do so.

00:09:45.349 --> 00:09:47.647
And l want to give that order.

00:09:47.685 --> 00:09:50.245
But you have to tell me...

00:09:50.287 --> 00:09:53.950
where is Tedran?

00:09:53.991 --> 00:09:57.051
He's here, at these coordinates.

00:09:57.094 --> 00:09:59.756
Assuming our prisoner
told you the truth.

00:09:59.797 --> 00:10:02.766
Oh, believe me, he was
very cooperative at the end.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:03.960
Neelix?

00:10:04.001 --> 00:10:05.628
L'm reading
a fortified compound

00:10:05.669 --> 00:10:08.160
1.6 kilometers
beneath the surface.

00:10:08.205 --> 00:10:11.106
Chako-tay, you and Tuvok
take an assault team

00:10:11.141 --> 00:10:13.632
and find Tedran.

00:10:13.677 --> 00:10:16.339
Make sure he's escorted
safely to Voyager.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.438
Yes, sir.

00:10:18.649 --> 00:10:20.014
What now?

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:23.349
Intruders. Four Kyrians just
beamed into the Engine Room.

00:10:23.387 --> 00:10:24.877
Bridge to Engineering.

00:10:24.922 --> 00:10:26.480
Respond.

00:10:26.523 --> 00:10:29.356
They've erected force fields.

00:10:29.393 --> 00:10:31.384
Our soldiers can't get in.

00:10:32.897 --> 00:10:35.263
They've left me no choice.

00:10:35.299 --> 00:10:36.596
Computer...

00:10:36.634 --> 00:10:39.865
initiate the Borg
activation sequence.

00:10:39.904 --> 00:10:41.872
Sequence in progress.

00:10:41.906 --> 00:10:45.171
Bridge to Seven of Nine.

00:10:45.209 --> 00:10:46.699
State your instructions.

00:10:46.744 --> 00:10:50.180
A group of Kyrians
is in the Engine Room.

00:10:50.214 --> 00:10:51.681
Stop them.

00:10:51.715 --> 00:10:53.945
We understand.

00:11:22.446 --> 00:11:25.210
Resistance is futile.

00:11:25.249 --> 00:11:27.342
Seven of Nine to the Bridge.

00:11:27.384 --> 00:11:30.285
The Kyrian threat
has been neutralized.

00:11:30.321 --> 00:11:31.583
Acknowledged.

00:11:31.622 --> 00:11:33.988
Two of the Kyrians
are still alive.

00:11:34.024 --> 00:11:35.889
What shall we do with them?

00:11:35.926 --> 00:11:39.794
Well, you've been wanting
to expand your fighting force.

00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:41.127
Assimilate them.

00:11:41.165 --> 00:11:44.396
We understand.

00:11:44.435 --> 00:11:47.893
L just received word
from the attack team.

00:11:47.938 --> 00:11:49.462
Good news, Lieutenant?

00:11:49.506 --> 00:11:50.700
Very.

00:11:50.741 --> 00:11:53.539
They've captured Tedran
and one of his aides.

00:11:53.577 --> 00:11:55.636
They're heading back
to Voyager.

00:11:57.314 --> 00:11:59.077
Take them to Chamber 19

00:11:59.116 --> 00:12:01.346
and get the Vaskan Ambassador.

00:12:01.385 --> 00:12:04.946
This is one negotiation
he won't want to miss.

00:12:15.766 --> 00:12:17.097
Welcome aboard.

00:12:17.134 --> 00:12:19.762
L appreciate your hospitality.

00:12:19.803 --> 00:12:23.034
Are all your guests
treated so well?

00:12:23.073 --> 00:12:24.370
Well, it's not every day

00:12:24.408 --> 00:12:26.876
that we receive
such an important visitor...

00:12:26.944 --> 00:12:28.172
the great Tedran...

00:12:28.212 --> 00:12:31.545
a man of wisdom and peace...

00:12:31.582 --> 00:12:33.209
a servant of his people.

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:36.651
Well, your people need you,
now more than ever.

00:12:36.687 --> 00:12:39.417
State your demands.

00:12:39.456 --> 00:12:44.519
Tell your forces to stand down,
and l'll call off my attack.

00:12:44.561 --> 00:12:47.997
L understand
what the Vaskans want...

00:12:48.032 --> 00:12:50.660
more of our territory...

00:12:50.701 --> 00:12:52.100
more resources.

00:12:52.136 --> 00:12:54.900
But what do you want, Captain?

00:12:54.938 --> 00:12:57.634
Why are you doing this to us?

00:12:57.674 --> 00:13:00.302
He's offered my crew a way home.

00:13:00.344 --> 00:13:03.980
To reach your home,
you would destroy ours?

00:13:04.113 --> 00:13:05.273
That's right.

00:13:05.314 --> 00:13:08.010
And you'd do the same
in my position.

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:10.985
No, l would not.

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:15.047
Spoken like a true martyr.

00:13:15.091 --> 00:13:17.525
You're very enlightened.

00:13:20.096 --> 00:13:23.554
But are you so proud...

00:13:23.599 --> 00:13:29.037
that you'd let your people die
before you'd humble yourself?

00:13:33.409 --> 00:13:35.206
Tell them to surrender.

00:13:37.079 --> 00:13:39.047
You have shamed us all.

00:13:39.081 --> 00:13:41.481
We could've ended this
on our own...

00:13:41.517 --> 00:13:42.882
peacefully...

00:13:42.985 --> 00:13:44.680
without her.

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:46.517
Surrender.

00:13:49.025 --> 00:13:50.356
No.

00:14:05.374 --> 00:14:09.242
We will prevail.

00:14:18.254 --> 00:14:21.246
Don't look so shocked,
Ambassador.

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:24.088
This is what you wanted,
isn't it?

00:14:34.336 --> 00:14:37.305
The ensuing conflict
was brief but brutal...

00:14:37.339 --> 00:14:40.502
two million Kyrians
slaughtered within days.

00:14:42.511 --> 00:14:45.002
The Warship Voyager
continued on its way,

00:14:45.047 --> 00:14:47.277
leaving the Kyrian dynasty
in ruins.

00:14:47.316 --> 00:14:50.285
The Vaskan leaders proceeded
to occupy our lands,

00:14:50.319 --> 00:14:52.549
forcing my people
into subservience.

00:14:52.588 --> 00:14:55.284
It took centuries for us
to undo the damage

00:14:55.324 --> 00:14:57.189
that Captain Janeway had done.

00:14:57.226 --> 00:15:00.627
And the Kyrian struggle
for equality is far from over.

00:15:00.663 --> 00:15:02.597
This simulation and this museum

00:15:02.631 --> 00:15:04.997
are a testament
to that struggle.

00:15:05.034 --> 00:15:07.594
L hope you found
your experience here worthwhile.

00:15:07.636 --> 00:15:09.729
If you'd like to learn
more about Voyager

00:15:09.772 --> 00:15:12.036
and its role
in the history of our planet,

00:15:12.074 --> 00:15:14.474
l suggest you explore
the rest of this exhibit.

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:15.670
Thank you for your time.

00:15:38.467 --> 00:15:40.435
Please, feel free
to try the simulation.

00:15:40.469 --> 00:15:42.266
Oh, thank you very much.

00:15:46.375 --> 00:15:48.400
L wouldn't touch
that if l were you.

00:15:48.444 --> 00:15:51.675
One of the Voyager's torpedoes...
25-isoton yield.

00:15:51.714 --> 00:15:54.478
It could destroy an entire city
within seconds.

00:15:54.517 --> 00:15:56.382
It's been inactive
for centuries,

00:15:56.418 --> 00:15:57.749
but you never know.

00:15:57.786 --> 00:16:00.619
No, l'm only teasing,
but, please, be careful.

00:16:00.656 --> 00:16:02.521
If we damage
any of these relics,

00:16:02.558 --> 00:16:04.116
they can never be replaced.

00:16:04.160 --> 00:16:06.822
The history of our people
should be respected.

00:16:06.929 --> 00:16:09.124
L have a question
about that history.

00:16:09.165 --> 00:16:10.154
Please.

00:16:10.199 --> 00:16:12.497
How can you prove
that it's true?

00:16:12.535 --> 00:16:14.935
Take a closer look.

00:16:14.970 --> 00:16:16.631
The evidence is all around you.

00:16:16.672 --> 00:16:19.004
Some musty fossils
and a re-creation?

00:16:19.041 --> 00:16:20.565
That doesn't prove anything.

00:16:20.609 --> 00:16:23.169
L disagree.

00:16:23.212 --> 00:16:24.679
You're trying
to blame the Vaskans

00:16:24.713 --> 00:16:26.704
for all your troubles,
the way you always do.

00:16:26.749 --> 00:16:29.411
L don't have a problem
with your species.

00:16:29.451 --> 00:16:32.818
L have Kyrian friends,
but l don't appreciate

00:16:32.855 --> 00:16:35.085
seeing my people
being portrayed as villains

00:16:35.124 --> 00:16:38.150
in your little simulation,
and l certainly don't want

00:16:38.194 --> 00:16:40.094
your history taught
to my children.

00:16:40.129 --> 00:16:42.791
Well, you'd better
get used to the idea,

00:16:42.831 --> 00:16:44.958
because we've just uncovered
an artifact that's going

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:46.991
to confirm everything
you've seen here.

00:16:47.036 --> 00:16:48.230
Three weeks ago,

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:50.738
our research team
found a data-storage device

00:16:50.773 --> 00:16:53.333
buried nine meters
beneath the ruins at Kesef.

00:16:53.375 --> 00:16:55.639
L've confirmed
that it came from Voyager.

00:16:55.678 --> 00:16:57.475
Another fossil?

00:16:57.513 --> 00:16:59.572
The device contains
active data...

00:16:59.615 --> 00:17:00.877
possibly crew logs...

00:17:00.983 --> 00:17:03.474
even Captain Janeway's
personal almanac.

00:17:03.519 --> 00:17:04.918
In the next few days,
we could be hearing

00:17:04.954 --> 00:17:06.216
Voyager's version
of these events,

00:17:06.255 --> 00:17:07.552
in their own words!

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:09.490
And what if those words
tell a different story?

00:17:09.525 --> 00:17:10.822
What then?

00:17:12.294 --> 00:17:14.819
We will change our views
accordingly.

00:17:14.863 --> 00:17:17.024
L'm sure you will.

00:17:21.670 --> 00:17:22.796
L apologize.

00:17:22.838 --> 00:17:25.466
Please, enjoy
the rest of your visit.

00:17:45.694 --> 00:17:49.152
Activate re-creation:
"The Voyager Encounter."

00:17:49.198 --> 00:17:50.825
Display Engine Room.

00:18:07.149 --> 00:18:08.411
Begin dictation.

00:18:09.985 --> 00:18:13.386
L'm resuming work
on artifact 271:

00:18:13.422 --> 00:18:15.788
The Voyager data-storage device.

00:18:17.159 --> 00:18:20.094
L've decided to try
using period tools

00:18:20.129 --> 00:18:22.495
from the simulation itself.

00:18:22.531 --> 00:18:26.160
With any luck,
they'll be more compatible.

00:18:35.678 --> 00:18:36.940
Hmm...

00:18:36.979 --> 00:18:39.914
there's far more data here
than l expected.

00:18:43.652 --> 00:18:46.519
Seems more like a program
of some sort.

00:18:48.524 --> 00:18:49.491
Yes.

00:18:49.525 --> 00:18:50.651
Yes!

00:18:50.693 --> 00:18:53.821
Lt's an optronic datastream...

00:18:53.862 --> 00:18:55.295
a hologram.

00:19:07.142 --> 00:19:10.202
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:19:12.815 --> 00:19:15.750
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:19:17.152 --> 00:19:18.983
L recognize you.

00:19:19.021 --> 00:19:20.352
You're Voyager's Doctor.

00:19:20.389 --> 00:19:21.947
What am l doing in Engineering?

00:19:23.559 --> 00:19:25.424
Where's my mobile emitter?

00:19:25.461 --> 00:19:26.792
You're not an android.

00:19:26.829 --> 00:19:27.796
Of course not.

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:29.559
What are you talking about?

00:19:29.598 --> 00:19:30.826
A Kyrian.

00:19:30.933 --> 00:19:33.231
Doctor to the Bridge.
Intruder alert!

00:19:33.268 --> 00:19:34.792
Security to Engineering!

00:19:34.837 --> 00:19:36.737
You won't have
much luck with that.

00:19:36.772 --> 00:19:38.103
Nothing in here is real.

00:19:38.140 --> 00:19:39.368
It's a simulation.

00:19:40.843 --> 00:19:41.810
A holodeck?

00:19:41.844 --> 00:19:42.936
No.

00:19:42.978 --> 00:19:45.105
You're in the Museum
of Kyrian Heritage.

00:19:45.147 --> 00:19:47.775
You've stolen my program.

00:19:47.816 --> 00:19:48.783
How?

00:19:48.817 --> 00:19:49.784
Please...

00:19:49.818 --> 00:19:51.376
let me try to explain.

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:52.944
Try quickly.

00:19:52.988 --> 00:19:54.785
You...

00:19:54.823 --> 00:19:56.791
are a hologram.

00:19:56.825 --> 00:19:58.383
That l know.

00:19:58.427 --> 00:20:00.622
Uh... l just discovered
your program

00:20:00.662 --> 00:20:02.687
inside this data-storage device.

00:20:02.731 --> 00:20:04.392
That's the EMH backup module.

00:20:04.433 --> 00:20:07.369
One of your attack parties must
have taken it from Sick Bay.

00:20:07.502 --> 00:20:09.697
Actually, we found it
at the ruins at Kesef.

00:20:11.339 --> 00:20:14.399
L know this will be difficult
for you to accept,

00:20:14.442 --> 00:20:16.706
but a great deal
of time has passed

00:20:16.745 --> 00:20:19.145
since Voyager
encountered the Kyrians.

00:20:19.180 --> 00:20:21.478
How much time?

00:20:21.516 --> 00:20:24.849
700 years,
give or take a decade.

00:20:24.886 --> 00:20:26.148
We're not certain.

00:20:26.187 --> 00:20:27.586
L don't believe you.

00:20:27.622 --> 00:20:28.680
Think about it.

00:20:28.723 --> 00:20:30.486
When your program is inactive,

00:20:30.525 --> 00:20:33.392
a moment or a millennium
are the same to you.

00:20:37.899 --> 00:20:39.730
700 years?

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:43.799
What about my ship?

00:20:43.838 --> 00:20:46.033
What happened to my crew?

00:20:46.074 --> 00:20:47.063
No one knows.

00:20:47.108 --> 00:20:49.576
It's safe to say
they're long dead.

00:20:51.579 --> 00:20:54.810
And l'm some sort of...
fossil?

00:20:54.849 --> 00:20:56.339
No, not a fossil...

00:20:56.384 --> 00:21:01.185
a witness, a living witness
to history.

00:21:01.222 --> 00:21:03.782
There's so much we don't know
about what happened,

00:21:03.825 --> 00:21:05.224
but you saw it.

00:21:05.260 --> 00:21:07.956
You lived through those times.

00:21:07.996 --> 00:21:10.692
You helped to shape them.

00:21:10.732 --> 00:21:13.098
Doctor, you could be
the most important discovery

00:21:13.134 --> 00:21:14.101
of all time.

00:21:14.135 --> 00:21:15.500
No, this isn't possible.

00:21:15.537 --> 00:21:16.504
Doctor...

00:21:16.538 --> 00:21:17.835
l don't believe you.

00:21:17.872 --> 00:21:18.861
Doctor!

00:21:44.365 --> 00:21:46.890
What's going to happen
to me now?

00:21:46.968 --> 00:21:49.027
Will you put me on display?

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:51.504
The holographic Rip van Winkle?

00:21:51.539 --> 00:21:52.836
L'm not sure.

00:21:52.874 --> 00:21:55.104
L want to try
to contact Starfleet...

00:21:55.143 --> 00:21:56.906
if there still is a Starfleet.

00:21:56.978 --> 00:21:58.411
That will have to wait.

00:21:58.446 --> 00:21:59.743
Wait for what?

00:21:59.781 --> 00:22:02.147
There are other...
issues to be resolved.

00:22:02.183 --> 00:22:03.480
What kind of issues?

00:22:03.518 --> 00:22:05.008
You're the Voyager Doctor.

00:22:05.053 --> 00:22:07.453
A lot of people are going
to have questions.

00:22:07.489 --> 00:22:08.683
On our world,

00:22:08.723 --> 00:22:11.453
artificial life-forms
are considered sentient

00:22:11.493 --> 00:22:13.552
and responsible
for their actions.

00:22:13.595 --> 00:22:15.495
You might have to face charges.

00:22:15.530 --> 00:22:16.656
Charges?

00:22:16.698 --> 00:22:17.722
For your crimes.

00:22:17.765 --> 00:22:19.164
You designed the bio-weapons

00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:21.031
that killed
eight million Kyrians.

00:22:21.069 --> 00:22:23.196
L did nothing of the sort.

00:22:23.238 --> 00:22:25.763
All of our evidence shows
that you were a war criminal.

00:22:25.807 --> 00:22:27.138
Evidence? What evidence?

00:22:27.175 --> 00:22:29.370
Like this, for example?
Triple-armored hull?

00:22:29.410 --> 00:22:31.173
30 torpedo tubes?
25 phaser banks?

00:22:31.212 --> 00:22:33.180
This isn't what our ship
looked like.

00:22:33.214 --> 00:22:35.614
We reconstructed it
from a partial schematic

00:22:35.650 --> 00:22:37.242
found in the Cyrik Ocean...

00:22:37.285 --> 00:22:38.843
which was badly damaged
by corrosion.

00:22:38.887 --> 00:22:40.752
We were bound to get
a few details wrong.

00:22:40.788 --> 00:22:42.813
Voyager wasn't a warship.

00:22:42.857 --> 00:22:44.256
We were explorers!

00:22:44.292 --> 00:22:46.817
Yes, l know...
trying to get home, to Mars.

00:22:46.861 --> 00:22:49.796
Earth! You see, you couldn't
even get that right!

00:22:49.831 --> 00:22:51.298
This is a nightmare.

00:22:51.332 --> 00:22:53.095
What if l'm found guilty?

00:22:53.134 --> 00:22:55.193
What's going to happen to me?

00:22:55.236 --> 00:22:57.170
That's up to the Arbiters.

00:22:57.205 --> 00:22:59.105
But l imagine
the penalty would be severe.

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:02.200
Your program
could be decompiled.

00:23:02.243 --> 00:23:04.336
You've got to believe me.

00:23:04.379 --> 00:23:06.847
To you, this may be
ancient history.

00:23:06.915 --> 00:23:08.780
To me, it's yesterday.

00:23:08.816 --> 00:23:10.841
You called me a living witness.

00:23:10.885 --> 00:23:12.182
Well, at least
give me the chance

00:23:12.220 --> 00:23:13.619
to set the record straight.

00:23:13.655 --> 00:23:16.783
L want to see your version
of what happened.

00:23:16.891 --> 00:23:18.859
We've already drained
two phaser banks,

00:23:18.960 --> 00:23:20.018
and he hasn't hit anything.

00:23:20.061 --> 00:23:22.529
If you looked at your
console once in awhile,

00:23:22.564 --> 00:23:24.498
instead of chasing
the female ensigns,

00:23:24.532 --> 00:23:25.760
you'd see otherwise.

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:26.789
Tom's right.

00:23:26.834 --> 00:23:27.801
This war was supposed

00:23:27.835 --> 00:23:29.029
to be over in five minutes.

00:23:29.070 --> 00:23:31.004
You have a better idea,
Lieutenant?

00:23:31.039 --> 00:23:32.472
As a matter of fact, l do.

00:23:32.507 --> 00:23:35.032
Fighter shuttles...
a direct assault.

00:23:35.076 --> 00:23:37.340
Led by you? Good luck.

00:23:37.378 --> 00:23:39.209
Watch your mouth, hedgehog.

00:23:39.247 --> 00:23:40.874
L haven't heard
a single good idea.

00:23:40.982 --> 00:23:43.883
Well, then propose something,
First Officer.

00:23:43.918 --> 00:23:45.545
Earn your rank for once.

00:23:47.422 --> 00:23:49.652
Get away from us...

00:23:51.392 --> 00:23:53.189
Gentlemen...

00:23:53.227 --> 00:23:55.195
Gentlemen!

00:23:58.566 --> 00:24:04.505
Save it for the holodeck...
we've got a war to fight.

00:24:04.539 --> 00:24:06.666
We've only been attacking

00:24:06.708 --> 00:24:10.508
the Kyrian military
installations... a mistake.

00:24:10.545 --> 00:24:13.343
We should target
the general population.

00:24:13.381 --> 00:24:15.349
Excellent idea, Captain.

00:24:15.383 --> 00:24:16.577
L've examined
the Kyrian genome,

00:24:16.618 --> 00:24:17.642
and they would be vulnerable

00:24:17.685 --> 00:24:19.050
to any number
of biological weapons.

00:24:19.087 --> 00:24:21.521
How soon could you
have one ready?

00:24:21.556 --> 00:24:23.683
Within the hour.

00:24:25.693 --> 00:24:28.321
Dismissed.

00:24:28.363 --> 00:24:29.853
Pure fiction.

00:24:29.897 --> 00:24:31.694
This is absurd.

00:24:31.733 --> 00:24:33.360
Halt re-creation.

00:24:33.401 --> 00:24:35.801
This is
a reasonable extrapolation

00:24:35.837 --> 00:24:37.099
from historic record.

00:24:37.138 --> 00:24:38.571
But if you'd like

00:24:38.606 --> 00:24:40.506
to point out
any inconsistencies...

00:24:40.541 --> 00:24:41.667
Inconsistencies?!

00:24:41.709 --> 00:24:43.267
L don't know where to begin.

00:24:43.311 --> 00:24:45.779
Granted, this looks
like the briefing room,

00:24:45.813 --> 00:24:47.838
but these aren't
the people l knew.

00:24:47.882 --> 00:24:50.180
No one behaved like this.

00:24:50.218 --> 00:24:52.880
Well... aside from Mr. Paris.

00:24:52.920 --> 00:24:55.218
We weren't
at each other's throats.

00:24:55.256 --> 00:24:56.883
We didn't talk about
how to destroy planets.

00:24:56.991 --> 00:24:57.889
We helped people.

00:24:57.992 --> 00:25:00.119
We were an enlightened crew.

00:25:00.161 --> 00:25:02.322
Are you denying
these events took place?

00:25:02.363 --> 00:25:03.489
Yes.

00:25:03.531 --> 00:25:04.828
Are you saying
you never got involved

00:25:04.866 --> 00:25:06.060
in the conflict
between my people

00:25:06.100 --> 00:25:08.068
- and the Vaskans?
- Yes!

00:25:08.102 --> 00:25:09.660
Well, no, we did get involved,

00:25:09.704 --> 00:25:11.331
but it was nothing like this.

00:25:11.372 --> 00:25:12.361
Elaborate.

00:25:14.108 --> 00:25:16.838
There was a meeting
in this room,

00:25:16.878 --> 00:25:19.278
but it wasn't
about battle tactics,

00:25:19.313 --> 00:25:22.009
it was about a dilemma
we were facing.

00:25:23.885 --> 00:25:26.854
We had negotiated a trade
agreement with the Vaskans.

00:25:26.921 --> 00:25:30.049
We were dealing with
a representative, Ambassador...

00:25:30.091 --> 00:25:31.388
Ambassador Daleth.

00:25:31.426 --> 00:25:33.087
Daleth. Exactly.

00:25:35.029 --> 00:25:38.692
Everything was going
according to plan...

00:25:38.733 --> 00:25:40.826
until...

00:25:42.637 --> 00:25:44.332
...we were attacked...

00:25:44.372 --> 00:25:46.966
by your people, the Kyrians.

00:25:47.008 --> 00:25:49.306
They'd picked that moment
to start a war

00:25:49.343 --> 00:25:51.106
and we were caught
in the middle.

00:25:51.145 --> 00:25:52.669
The Kyrians were the aggressors?

00:25:52.714 --> 00:25:54.648
No, no, that can't be right.

00:25:54.682 --> 00:25:56.309
Captain Janeway called
this meeting to figure out

00:25:56.350 --> 00:25:58.045
how we could extricate ourselves
from the conflict

00:25:58.086 --> 00:26:00.520
and still maintain the trade
agreement with the Vaskans.

00:26:00.555 --> 00:26:02.284
But we weren't on their side,

00:26:02.323 --> 00:26:04.416
and we certainly
never attacked you.

00:26:04.459 --> 00:26:08.555
Save your objections until
you see the entire re-creation.

00:26:08.596 --> 00:26:09.927
Let's continue.

00:26:11.833 --> 00:26:14.131
We will prevail.

00:26:23.277 --> 00:26:25.142
Don't look so shocked,
Ambassador.

00:26:25.179 --> 00:26:27.511
This is what you wanted,
isn't it?

00:26:35.957 --> 00:26:40.826
Somewhere... halfway
across the galaxy, l hope...

00:26:40.862 --> 00:26:44.059
Captain Janeway
is spinning in her grave.

00:26:44.098 --> 00:26:45.861
You've portrayed us as monsters.

00:26:45.933 --> 00:26:47.867
The Captain's
a cold-blooded killer;

00:26:47.935 --> 00:26:50.961
the crew's a gang of thugs;
and l'm a mass murderer.

00:26:51.005 --> 00:26:52.836
- Calm yourself.
- Why should I?

00:26:52.874 --> 00:26:55.240
L'm about to be hanged
for crimes l didn't commit.

00:26:55.276 --> 00:26:57.676
Tell me your version of events.

00:27:02.483 --> 00:27:04.508
L remember this man.

00:27:04.552 --> 00:27:05.678
Tedran.

00:27:05.720 --> 00:27:07.381
He was a martyr to our people.

00:27:07.421 --> 00:27:08.581
Some martyr.

00:27:08.623 --> 00:27:11.217
He led the Kyrian attack
against Voyager.

00:27:11.259 --> 00:27:12.317
You're lying.

00:27:12.360 --> 00:27:13.418
L was there.

00:27:13.461 --> 00:27:15.486
You're trying
to protect yourself.

00:27:15.530 --> 00:27:16.827
And so are you!

00:27:16.864 --> 00:27:18.165
From the truth.

00:27:18.298 --> 00:27:20.027
Isn't it a coincidence
that the Kyrians are

00:27:20.066 --> 00:27:22.193
being portrayed
in the best possible light?

00:27:22.235 --> 00:27:26.296
Martyrs, heroes, saviors.

00:27:26.339 --> 00:27:27.829
Obviously, events
have been reinterpreted

00:27:27.908 --> 00:27:30.399
to make your people
feel better about themselves.

00:27:30.443 --> 00:27:32.604
Revisionist history...

00:27:32.646 --> 00:27:34.079
it's such a comfort.

00:27:34.114 --> 00:27:36.139
We were not the aggressors
in the Great War.

00:27:36.183 --> 00:27:37.616
We were the victims.

00:27:37.651 --> 00:27:40.142
The proof can be found
anywhere on this world.

00:27:40.187 --> 00:27:42.951
The Kyrian people are
being oppressed to this day.

00:27:42.989 --> 00:27:45.287
The problems in your society
are none of my business.

00:27:45.325 --> 00:27:48.726
L'm just telling you
what l saw 700 years ago.

00:27:48.762 --> 00:27:51.856
L don't believe you,
and neither will anyone else.

00:27:51.932 --> 00:27:52.956
What are you doing?

00:27:52.999 --> 00:27:54.466
Shutting down your program.

00:27:54.501 --> 00:27:55.798
Wait. Please. I...

00:27:55.835 --> 00:27:57.166
l can prove to you l'm right.

00:27:57.204 --> 00:27:58.296
The medical tricorder...

00:27:58.338 --> 00:27:59.862
the artifact
you have on display.

00:27:59.940 --> 00:28:01.032
If you just let me...

00:28:06.546 --> 00:28:07.911
Lies.

00:28:19.259 --> 00:28:22.160
Begin dictation.

00:28:22.195 --> 00:28:24.425
L've reexamined the data module

00:28:24.464 --> 00:28:28.025
and from what l can tell, the
Doctor was telling the truth...

00:28:28.068 --> 00:28:30.969
at least about one thing.

00:28:31.004 --> 00:28:36.169
He is a hologram,
a backup program.

00:28:36.209 --> 00:28:38.700
We always knew he was
an artificial life-form,

00:28:38.745 --> 00:28:41.145
but we thought
he was an android.

00:28:44.184 --> 00:28:47.745
If we were mistaken
about that...

00:28:47.787 --> 00:28:50.847
l wonder if we might also
be wrong about Voyager itself.

00:28:54.194 --> 00:28:56.526
Another question:

00:28:56.563 --> 00:28:59.498
Why would a hologram
designed for medical purposes

00:28:59.532 --> 00:29:02.899
be programmed to lie so readily?

00:29:02.936 --> 00:29:04.233
From the moment l activated him,

00:29:04.271 --> 00:29:07.468
this Doctor has insisted
that he's innocent.

00:29:07.507 --> 00:29:10.908
At first, I...
didn't believe him.

00:29:14.581 --> 00:29:16.572
End dictation.

00:29:38.605 --> 00:29:42.735
Activate re-creation:
"The Voyager Encounter."

00:29:42.776 --> 00:29:44.937
Display Medical Chamber.

00:29:56.456 --> 00:29:59.084
Please state the nature
of the medical...

00:29:59.125 --> 00:30:01.992
Oh. It's you.

00:30:03.630 --> 00:30:06.190
You've given me a lot
to think about.

00:30:06.232 --> 00:30:07.358
Really?

00:30:07.400 --> 00:30:10.995
L thought you'd heard enough
of my... lies.

00:30:11.037 --> 00:30:12.595
L judged you too quickly.

00:30:12.639 --> 00:30:13.606
L'm sorry.

00:30:13.640 --> 00:30:15.369
What changed your mind?

00:30:15.408 --> 00:30:18.275
Time to think.

00:30:18.311 --> 00:30:20.677
For your information,
l don't appreciate

00:30:20.714 --> 00:30:23.512
being deactivated
in the middle of a sentence.

00:30:23.550 --> 00:30:25.347
It brings back...

00:30:25.385 --> 00:30:26.852
unpleasant memories.

00:30:26.886 --> 00:30:28.046
It won't happen again.

00:30:28.088 --> 00:30:29.282
Good.

00:30:29.322 --> 00:30:30.414
Because if you don't stop
treating me

00:30:30.457 --> 00:30:31.424
like a second-class hologram,

00:30:31.458 --> 00:30:33.756
l won't cooperate
with your investigation.

00:30:33.793 --> 00:30:35.556
L'm perfectly happy
to lie dormant

00:30:35.595 --> 00:30:37.222
in that data module
for a few eons.

00:30:37.263 --> 00:30:38.696
L didn't come here to argue.

00:30:38.732 --> 00:30:40.222
Then what do you want?

00:30:41.501 --> 00:30:43.469
L don't know.

00:30:43.503 --> 00:30:46.301
To talk, l guess,

00:30:46.339 --> 00:30:50.070
about what really happened
700 years ago.

00:30:50.110 --> 00:30:51.509
Are you sure
you're willing to listen

00:30:51.544 --> 00:30:54.570
to a mass-murderer like me?

00:30:54.614 --> 00:30:56.775
L'm willing to keep
an open mind.

00:30:56.816 --> 00:30:58.647
That's the most l can promise.

00:31:00.186 --> 00:31:02.518
Try to understand
my point of view.

00:31:02.555 --> 00:31:05.251
All my life, l thought
l knew the truth.

00:31:05.291 --> 00:31:07.088
There was never any doubt.

00:31:07.127 --> 00:31:09.857
L never meant to throw
your beliefs into doubt,

00:31:09.896 --> 00:31:12.262
but l can't deny
what l know to be true.

00:31:12.298 --> 00:31:14.266
L realize that now...

00:31:14.300 --> 00:31:17.098
and l want to know the truth.

00:31:17.137 --> 00:31:20.334
And l want the Arbiters
to know it, too.

00:31:20.373 --> 00:31:22.864
Well...

00:31:22.909 --> 00:31:26.777
the stage is certainly set,

00:31:26.813 --> 00:31:29.111
but l'll have to rewrite
the characters

00:31:29.149 --> 00:31:30.878
and revise the plot a little.

00:31:30.950 --> 00:31:33.441
L'm quite adept in the art
of holographic programming.

00:31:33.486 --> 00:31:35.545
If you'll give me access
to your technology,

00:31:35.588 --> 00:31:38.523
maybe l can create
a simulation of my own...

00:31:38.558 --> 00:31:40.458
show you what happened.

00:31:43.563 --> 00:31:45.030
Don't worry, Ambassador.

00:31:45.064 --> 00:31:46.895
We've got plenty
of medical supplies,

00:31:46.966 --> 00:31:49.434
and we'd be more than happy
to share them with you.

00:31:49.469 --> 00:31:50.663
Then we agree.

00:31:50.703 --> 00:31:52.364
In exchange, we'll provide you

00:31:52.405 --> 00:31:54.396
with as much dilithium
as you need.

00:31:54.441 --> 00:31:56.306
That's very generous,
Ambassador.

00:31:56.342 --> 00:31:58.810
L'll transport the canisters
immediately.

00:31:58.845 --> 00:32:00.676
It would be
in your best interest

00:32:00.713 --> 00:32:02.340
to make this exchange quickly.

00:32:02.382 --> 00:32:03.349
Oh? Why is that?

00:32:03.383 --> 00:32:04.509
We've been in conflict

00:32:04.551 --> 00:32:06.781
with a neighboring species,
the Kyrians.

00:32:06.820 --> 00:32:09.152
They've been threatening
to attack us.

00:32:09.189 --> 00:32:11.680
War could break out any day.

00:32:11.724 --> 00:32:13.851
We've tried
every diplomatic option,

00:32:13.927 --> 00:32:16.657
but the Kyrians are
a violent, stubborn people.

00:32:16.696 --> 00:32:21.156
No problem. L understand
what you're going through.

00:32:21.201 --> 00:32:23.431
L wish l could make you
one of our diplomats.

00:32:23.470 --> 00:32:26.303
You might have better luck
resolving this situation.

00:32:26.339 --> 00:32:28.102
Under different circumstances...

00:32:28.141 --> 00:32:29.574
Janeway to Sick Bay.

00:32:29.609 --> 00:32:30.871
This is the Doctor.

00:32:30.910 --> 00:32:34.676
Ambassador Daleth and l
have reached an agreement.

00:32:34.714 --> 00:32:36.011
Assemble the medical supplies.

00:32:36.049 --> 00:32:37.141
Done, Captain.

00:32:37.183 --> 00:32:39.048
The supplies are in Cargo Bay 1.

00:32:39.085 --> 00:32:41.451
Once we transport the supplies
to the surface, there may be...

00:32:43.056 --> 00:32:44.023
Red Alert.

00:32:44.057 --> 00:32:45.251
Captain Janeway to the Bridge.

00:32:48.528 --> 00:32:51.156
We're being fired on
by three ships.

00:32:51.197 --> 00:32:52.164
The Kyrians.

00:32:52.198 --> 00:32:53.165
Hail them.

00:32:53.199 --> 00:32:54.393
Channel open.

00:32:54.434 --> 00:32:56.095
This is Captain Janeway
of the Starship Voyager.

00:32:56.135 --> 00:32:57.102
We are not your enemies.

00:32:57.136 --> 00:33:00.105
Please break off your attack.

00:33:00.139 --> 00:33:02.403
They're not responding.

00:33:02.442 --> 00:33:05.843
L'd advise you
to retreat, Captain.

00:33:05.945 --> 00:33:07.742
Shields down to 86 percent.

00:33:07.780 --> 00:33:08.747
Break out of orbit.

00:33:08.781 --> 00:33:10.078
Put some distance between us.

00:33:10.116 --> 00:33:11.913
Yes, ma'am.

00:33:12.986 --> 00:33:13.953
Four intruders.

00:33:13.987 --> 00:33:15.352
They are in Engineering.

00:33:15.388 --> 00:33:17.322
Janeway to Engineering.

00:33:17.357 --> 00:33:18.585
B'Elanna, respond.

00:33:19.926 --> 00:33:21.393
Tuvok.

00:33:25.265 --> 00:33:28.063
Take as much of their technology
as you can.

00:33:28.101 --> 00:33:29.432
You will fail.

00:33:32.772 --> 00:33:34.103
Drop your weapons.

00:33:34.140 --> 00:33:35.732
Back away.

00:33:47.620 --> 00:33:49.281
- Tuvok to Janeway.
- Go ahead.

00:33:49.322 --> 00:33:51.517
The Kyrians have killed three
of the Engineering crew.

00:33:51.558 --> 00:33:52.889
They've taken Seven of Nine

00:33:52.959 --> 00:33:55.120
and one of the injured
crew members hostage.

00:33:55.161 --> 00:33:57.391
They're now on Deck 2,
Section 32.

00:33:57.430 --> 00:33:58.727
Acknowledged.

00:33:58.765 --> 00:34:01.029
Remember your offer
to make me a diplomat?

00:34:01.067 --> 00:34:03.331
Well, it looks like l don't
have much of a choice.

00:34:03.369 --> 00:34:04.836
Tell the Doctor
we have casualties.

00:34:04.871 --> 00:34:06.395
Have him meet us on Deck 2.

00:34:11.311 --> 00:34:12.278
Janeway to Tuvok.

00:34:12.312 --> 00:34:14.007
We're approaching Section 31.

00:34:14.047 --> 00:34:16.413
The evacuation of Deck 2
is complete.

00:34:16.449 --> 00:34:18.713
Send three security
teams to this deck,

00:34:18.751 --> 00:34:20.616
then seal all the access points.

00:34:20.653 --> 00:34:21.847
Acknowledged.

00:34:21.955 --> 00:34:23.252
How typical of the Kyrians.

00:34:23.289 --> 00:34:24.256
What do you mean?

00:34:24.290 --> 00:34:27.350
They fight the same way
they live... deviously.

00:34:32.531 --> 00:34:33.623
Janeway to Tuvok.

00:34:33.665 --> 00:34:34.723
Tuvok here.

00:34:34.767 --> 00:34:35.859
The Kyrians are
in the Mess Hall.

00:34:35.901 --> 00:34:36.868
We're going in.

00:34:36.902 --> 00:34:37.960
Security is on the way.

00:34:38.003 --> 00:34:39.868
L'll go first, Captain,
and draw any fire, if need be.

00:34:39.972 --> 00:34:41.098
Your crew is heroic, Captain.

00:34:41.140 --> 00:34:42.971
L just happen to be
invulnerable to phaser fire,

00:34:43.008 --> 00:34:44.236
but l appreciate the compliment.

00:34:44.276 --> 00:34:45.573
- Captain?
- Go.

00:34:48.547 --> 00:34:50.310
Tedran...

00:34:50.349 --> 00:34:51.441
this is between us.

00:34:51.483 --> 00:34:52.882
Leave these people out of it.

00:34:52.985 --> 00:34:54.612
L know what you're doing...

00:34:54.653 --> 00:34:56.746
an alliance with these aliens.

00:34:56.789 --> 00:34:58.484
We were trading with them,
nothing more.

00:34:58.524 --> 00:35:00.424
You expect me to believe that?

00:35:00.459 --> 00:35:03.360
You plan to use this ship
to destroy us.

00:35:03.395 --> 00:35:06.990
We wouldn't need help
if we wanted to destroy you.

00:35:07.032 --> 00:35:09.159
We didn't realize you were
fighting with the Vaskans.

00:35:09.201 --> 00:35:10.828
Now, lay down your weapons,

00:35:10.869 --> 00:35:13.303
and l promise
you won't be harmed.

00:35:18.544 --> 00:35:19.203
No!

00:35:29.988 --> 00:35:30.977
He's dead.

00:35:34.793 --> 00:35:37.091
Computer, freeze program.

00:35:37.129 --> 00:35:38.619
A tragic, needless death,

00:35:38.664 --> 00:35:41.861
but, as you can see,
Voyager was not responsible.

00:35:41.967 --> 00:35:43.559
After Tedran was killed,

00:35:43.602 --> 00:35:46.503
Voyager was attacked
by nine Kyrian ships.

00:35:46.538 --> 00:35:48.165
My program was disabled,

00:35:48.207 --> 00:35:50.869
most likely when they stole
my backup module.

00:35:50.909 --> 00:35:52.069
The next thing l knew,

00:35:52.110 --> 00:35:54.135
l was standing
next to this gentleman,

00:35:54.179 --> 00:35:55.407
seven centuries later.

00:35:55.447 --> 00:35:56.607
Very entertaining.

00:35:56.648 --> 00:35:58.309
L'll admit your holo-technology
is new to me.

00:35:58.350 --> 00:36:00.215
L had to extrapolate
in a few places,

00:36:00.252 --> 00:36:02.083
but l assure you, this is
an accurate re-creation.

00:36:02.120 --> 00:36:04.918
Perhaps. Or perhaps
it's the fabrication

00:36:04.957 --> 00:36:07.824
of a war criminal
who's afraid for his life.

00:36:07.926 --> 00:36:11.453
Do you have any evidence
to support your explanation?

00:36:11.497 --> 00:36:13.431
In fact, l do.

00:36:13.465 --> 00:36:17.162
L've confirmed that this
is the same tricorder

00:36:17.202 --> 00:36:19.830
l used to scan Tedran
at the moment of his death.

00:36:19.938 --> 00:36:22.065
If l can access
the bio-readings inside,

00:36:22.107 --> 00:36:24.473
l can prove that he was killed
by a Vaskan weapon,

00:36:24.510 --> 00:36:26.273
not by Captain Janeway.

00:36:26.311 --> 00:36:27.938
Can this be done?

00:36:27.980 --> 00:36:30.574
L've been trying to decipher
the instrument for years,

00:36:30.616 --> 00:36:32.106
but with the Doctor's help...

00:36:32.150 --> 00:36:33.674
l fail to see what
this would prove.

00:36:33.719 --> 00:36:35.550
Tedran died on Voyager,

00:36:35.587 --> 00:36:38.078
a victim of a conspiracy
to oppress my people.

00:36:38.123 --> 00:36:41.581
The weapon used, who fired it...
this is all beside the point.

00:36:41.627 --> 00:36:43.254
Was there a conspiracy?

00:36:43.295 --> 00:36:45.354
Did Voyager really help
my ancestors

00:36:45.397 --> 00:36:46.796
to start the Great War,

00:36:46.832 --> 00:36:48.823
or were Kyrians the aggressors,

00:36:48.867 --> 00:36:50.391
as my people have always
believed?

00:36:50.435 --> 00:36:53.165
No, this casts doubt
on everything.

00:36:53.205 --> 00:36:55.400
But it doesn't change
the fact that my children

00:36:55.440 --> 00:36:57.670
can't attend the same academies
as yours,

00:36:57.709 --> 00:37:01.270
or that we are forced to live
outside of the city center.

00:37:01.313 --> 00:37:03.804
Today's problems
are not at issue here.

00:37:03.849 --> 00:37:05.282
This is about history.

00:37:05.317 --> 00:37:07.478
Look, l don't know
who started your war.

00:37:07.519 --> 00:37:09.953
All l'm saying is that
Voyager wasn't responsible.

00:37:09.988 --> 00:37:12.821
L can't believe
that you would cooperate

00:37:12.858 --> 00:37:15.725
with this murderer...
you, of all people.

00:37:15.761 --> 00:37:16.955
You built this museum.

00:37:16.995 --> 00:37:20.226
The facts are turning out to be
more complex than l expected.

00:37:20.265 --> 00:37:22.927
We shouldn't be listening
to this hologram.

00:37:22.968 --> 00:37:24.731
L want him arrested and charged

00:37:24.770 --> 00:37:26.829
for the crimes
we know he committed.

00:37:26.939 --> 00:37:28.804
That's not your decision
to make.

00:37:28.840 --> 00:37:30.603
No, it's not, is it?

00:37:30.642 --> 00:37:32.109
L'm only on this commission

00:37:32.144 --> 00:37:34.078
because you needed
a token Kyrian.

00:37:34.112 --> 00:37:35.773
Please.
This isn't about race.

00:37:35.814 --> 00:37:37.111
It's always about race.

00:37:38.016 --> 00:37:40.109
You seize every opportunity

00:37:40.152 --> 00:37:42.347
to keep yourselves in power.

00:37:42.387 --> 00:37:43.945
L'm sorry you see it that way.

00:37:43.989 --> 00:37:45.286
L think we are obligated

00:37:45.324 --> 00:37:47.224
to hear what the Doctor
has to say.

00:37:47.259 --> 00:37:48.556
Proceed with your investigation.

00:37:48.594 --> 00:37:50.960
Yes, Arbiter.

00:37:52.497 --> 00:37:56.490
You'll pay for your crimes.

00:38:01.173 --> 00:38:03.539
700 years, and l'm still caught

00:38:03.575 --> 00:38:05.600
in the middle
of your little dispute.

00:38:05.644 --> 00:38:06.804
One might have hoped

00:38:06.912 --> 00:38:09.210
for a bit of social progress
in the interim.

00:38:09.247 --> 00:38:11.078
Change never comes
easily for us.

00:38:11.116 --> 00:38:12.811
Humph. That's an understatement.

00:38:12.918 --> 00:38:15.716
L've entered the specifications
that you gave me.

00:38:15.754 --> 00:38:17.915
Let's give it a try.

00:38:20.225 --> 00:38:21.385
Close enough.

00:38:21.426 --> 00:38:24.156
This diagnostic tool
should help me get past

00:38:24.196 --> 00:38:26.221
the initial
encryption sequences.

00:38:26.264 --> 00:38:28.562
Too bad we can't re-create
B'Elanna Torres.

00:38:28.600 --> 00:38:31.569
Torres... the Chief
Transporter Operator.

00:38:31.603 --> 00:38:33.230
Chief Engineer.

00:38:33.271 --> 00:38:34.704
You might want to make

00:38:34.740 --> 00:38:37.072
the correction
in your history books.

00:38:38.777 --> 00:38:40.438
What was she like... Torres?

00:38:40.479 --> 00:38:43.573
L suppose we've gotten
her personality wrong, too.

00:38:43.615 --> 00:38:45.640
Starting to believe
me, are you?

00:38:45.684 --> 00:38:50.678
Well, let's just say l'm
trying to keep an open mind.

00:38:50.722 --> 00:38:52.849
B'Elanna Torres...

00:38:52.891 --> 00:38:54.518
intelligent, beautiful,

00:38:54.559 --> 00:38:56.857
and with a chip on her shoulder

00:38:56.895 --> 00:38:59.728
the size
of the Horsehead Nebula.

00:38:59.765 --> 00:39:03.701
She also had
a kind of vulnerability

00:39:03.735 --> 00:39:05.464
that made her...

00:39:05.504 --> 00:39:07.369
quite endearing.

00:39:07.406 --> 00:39:09.067
You miss her...

00:39:09.107 --> 00:39:10.472
and the others.

00:39:10.509 --> 00:39:12.101
From my perspective,

00:39:12.144 --> 00:39:15.045
l saw them all
only a few days ago.

00:39:15.080 --> 00:39:17.810
But in fact,
it's been centuries.

00:39:17.916 --> 00:39:20.908
And l'll never see them again.

00:39:23.055 --> 00:39:26.252
Did they ever reach home?

00:39:26.291 --> 00:39:28.816
L wonder.

00:39:28.927 --> 00:39:30.724
L've always wondered that, too.

00:39:30.762 --> 00:39:33.925
From as far back
as l can remember.

00:39:33.965 --> 00:39:35.398
Really?

00:39:37.335 --> 00:39:39.701
Ever since
l was a small child,

00:39:39.738 --> 00:39:42.571
the first time l heard
the name Voyager,

00:39:42.607 --> 00:39:46.509
it conjured up my imagination.

00:39:46.545 --> 00:39:48.604
Even though we were
the bad guys?

00:39:48.647 --> 00:39:50.046
That didn't matter.

00:39:50.082 --> 00:39:53.711
L was too young
to understand the implications.

00:39:53.752 --> 00:39:56.380
The fact that you were
so far from home,

00:39:56.421 --> 00:39:58.855
traveling across the stars.

00:39:58.924 --> 00:40:01.859
Oh, l found it all very heroic.

00:40:01.960 --> 00:40:03.757
L suppose Voyager

00:40:03.795 --> 00:40:06.787
is what made me fall in love
with history.

00:40:06.832 --> 00:40:10.268
If it means anything to you,

00:40:10.302 --> 00:40:13.499
you would have made
a fine member of our crew.

00:40:19.111 --> 00:40:22.308
L hope that's part
of the simulation.

00:40:22.347 --> 00:40:24.315
No, it isn't.

00:41:05.957 --> 00:41:06.946
No! Stop this!

00:41:06.992 --> 00:41:08.425
We know about the hologram!

00:41:08.460 --> 00:41:10.087
This museum's filled with lies!

00:41:10.128 --> 00:41:11.493
Stop! Listen to me!

00:41:11.530 --> 00:41:13.054
We've listened long enough!

00:41:14.032 --> 00:41:16.660
They're using photon grenades.

00:41:16.701 --> 00:41:17.998
We've got to take cover.

00:41:18.036 --> 00:41:19.367
This way.

00:41:39.925 --> 00:41:40.892
What's happening?

00:41:40.992 --> 00:41:42.425
L've been hearing weapons.

00:41:42.460 --> 00:41:43.518
It's getting worse.

00:41:43.562 --> 00:41:44.824
Protests, vandalism...

00:41:44.863 --> 00:41:46.421
two people have been killed.

00:41:46.464 --> 00:41:48.022
Don't worry.
They've cordoned off the museum.

00:41:48.066 --> 00:41:49.431
We're safe for now.

00:41:49.467 --> 00:41:50.900
That's not
what l'm concerned about.

00:41:50.936 --> 00:41:53.530
Two deaths, a race riot,
all because of me?

00:41:55.407 --> 00:41:56.840
You were only the catalyst.

00:41:56.875 --> 00:41:58.775
The pressure's been
building for years.

00:41:58.810 --> 00:42:01.210
It was only a matter of time
before something set it off.

00:42:01.246 --> 00:42:02.440
Have you found the tricorder?

00:42:02.480 --> 00:42:03.447
Not yet.

00:42:03.481 --> 00:42:04.846
It's crucial that we do.

00:42:04.916 --> 00:42:08.217
The Kyrians are demanding
you be punished for your crimes,

00:42:08.350 --> 00:42:11.046
but the Vaskans want to hear
your version of events again.

00:42:11.086 --> 00:42:12.644
They want to continue
the investigation.

00:42:12.688 --> 00:42:14.212
What's going to happen?

00:42:14.256 --> 00:42:15.814
L don't know.

00:42:15.857 --> 00:42:19.258
The Vaskans are more powerful,
but the Kyrians are very angry.

00:42:19.294 --> 00:42:21.194
They're talking
about another war.

00:42:21.230 --> 00:42:23.994
Then there's only one solution.

00:42:24.032 --> 00:42:27.433
Delete my program.

00:42:27.469 --> 00:42:30.029
L've become a kind of symbol
for this conflict.

00:42:30.072 --> 00:42:31.232
As long as l'm around,

00:42:31.273 --> 00:42:34.174
your people are going
to keep on fighting.

00:42:34.209 --> 00:42:35.870
L'll show you
how to decompile my program.

00:42:35.944 --> 00:42:37.969
You can say l was damaged
in the attack last night.

00:42:38.013 --> 00:42:39.105
No one will hold you
responsible.

00:42:39.147 --> 00:42:40.341
L can't do that to you.

00:42:40.382 --> 00:42:41.713
Then l'll do it myself.

00:42:41.750 --> 00:42:42.717
No!

00:42:42.751 --> 00:42:44.241
L'm a medical hologram...

00:42:44.286 --> 00:42:45.776
programmed to do no harm,

00:42:45.821 --> 00:42:49.018
but l'm doing harm
on a global scale.

00:42:49.057 --> 00:42:51.025
Ever since you reactivated
me, l've been concerned

00:42:51.059 --> 00:42:52.890
with clearing
Voyager's good name.

00:42:52.961 --> 00:42:54.394
But that's not important now.

00:42:54.429 --> 00:42:55.726
There's more at stake.

00:42:55.764 --> 00:42:59.222
A few days ago,
l might have agreed with you.

00:42:59.268 --> 00:43:00.997
But what about the facts?

00:43:01.036 --> 00:43:02.503
Facts be damned!

00:43:02.537 --> 00:43:05.973
Names, dates, places...
it's all open to interpretation.

00:43:06.008 --> 00:43:08.340
Who's to say
what really happened?

00:43:08.377 --> 00:43:11.642
And ultimately,
what difference does it make?

00:43:11.680 --> 00:43:15.639
What matters is today and
the future of your people.

00:43:15.684 --> 00:43:17.015
Doctor, you were there.

00:43:17.052 --> 00:43:18.713
You can't deny what happened.

00:43:18.754 --> 00:43:22.019
L can... and l will.

00:43:22.057 --> 00:43:24.958
Tedran was a martyr
for your people, a hero,

00:43:24.993 --> 00:43:27.484
a symbol of your struggle
for freedom.

00:43:27.529 --> 00:43:29.724
Who am l to wander in
700 years later

00:43:29.765 --> 00:43:31.460
and take that away from you?

00:43:31.500 --> 00:43:33.434
History has been abused!

00:43:33.468 --> 00:43:36.869
We keep blaming each other
for what happened in the past.

00:43:36.972 --> 00:43:43.275
If you don't help us now,
it could be another 700 years.

00:43:48.083 --> 00:43:50.745
Let's find that tricorder.

00:44:03.732 --> 00:44:06.565
It was a pivotal moment
in our history.

00:44:09.371 --> 00:44:11.965
As a result
of the Doctor's testimony,

00:44:12.007 --> 00:44:15.340
a dialogue was opened
between our peoples.

00:44:15.377 --> 00:44:17.345
Eventually, we found
a new respect

00:44:17.379 --> 00:44:20.473
for our divergent cultures
and traditions.

00:44:20.515 --> 00:44:23.507
The efforts of people
like Quarren and the Doctor

00:44:23.552 --> 00:44:26.248
paved the way for unity.

00:44:26.288 --> 00:44:28.256
Quarren died six years later,

00:44:28.290 --> 00:44:32.818
but he lived long enough
to witness the Dawn of Harmony.

00:44:32.861 --> 00:44:34.260
And the Doctor...

00:44:34.296 --> 00:44:39.290
well, he served as our Surgical
Chancellor for many years,

00:44:39.334 --> 00:44:41.598
until he decided to leave.

00:44:41.636 --> 00:44:43.831
He took a small craft
and set a course

00:44:43.872 --> 00:44:45.669
for the Alpha Quadrant,

00:44:45.707 --> 00:44:48.870
attempting to trace
the path of Voyager.

00:44:48.977 --> 00:44:51.844
He said he had a longing...

00:44:51.880 --> 00:44:53.780
for home.

00:44:54.783 --> 00:44:56.216
This way.
